---
title: Chicken Piccata (Giada De Laurentiis)
servings: 4
prepTime: 15 min
cookTime: 25 min
difficulty: Easy
rating: 4
source: https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/giada-de-laurentiis/chicken-piccata-recipe2-1913809
tags: Chicken
---

> Chicken and sauce is a good flavor, chicken is moist.

For more even cooking and thinner fillets, optionally pound the @chicken breast tenders{1#lb}
flat between sheets of plastic wrap with a meat tenderizer or rolling pin.
Season the chicken with @salt and @pepper.

Place the @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup} in a shallow bowl for dredging.
Dredge chicken in flour and shake off excess.

In a #large skillet{} over medium high heat, melt 2 tablespoons of
@unsalted butter{6%tablespoons}(divided) with 3 tablespoons @olive oil{5%tablespoons}(divided).
When butter and oil start to sizzle, add 2 pieces of chicken and cook for ~{3%minutes}.
When chicken is browned, flip and cook other side for an additional 3 minutes.
Remove and transfer to plate.

Melt 2 more tablespoons butter and add another 2 tablespoons olive oil.
When butter and oil start to sizzle, add the other 2 pieces of chicken and brown both sides in same manner.
Remove pan from heat and add chicken to the plate.

Into the pan add the @lemon juice{1/4%cup}, @chicken stock{1/2%cup}, and @capers{1/4%cup}(drained and rinsed).
Return to stove and bring to boil, scraping up brown bits from the pan for extra flavor.
Check for seasoning.

Return all the chicken to the pan and simmer for ~{5%minutes}.
Remove chicken to platter.
Add remaining 2 tablespoons butter to sauce and whisk vigorously.
Pour sauce over chicken and serve.

